      "versionNonce": 1983670276,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788371667133,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "More e.g.",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "More e.g.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EEDnL18maKeO4EQkaQRxF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7303.819997255176,
      "y": -2673.6771686659254,
      "width": 801.0051851851802,
      "height": 181.99999999999977,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5ft",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1032169916,
      "version": 5027,
      "versionNonce": 916502204,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788371461340,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "now here you take the function out of the\nperson object, so fn() is called without an\nobject and this is not person \nso this is undefined",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "now here you take the function out of the person object, so fn() is called without an object and this is not person \nso this is undefined",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "c7DKM_R_GzJl3qlnCNxEj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8480.838947969365,
      "y": -2719.3914543802102,
      "width": 704.5995375700082,
      "height": 280.16666666666595,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5fv",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1791677828,
      "version": 5342,
      "versionNonce": 1013748668,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788372688438,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Therefore, the arrow function's parent\nlexical scope is the global scope (window in\nbrowsers, {} or module exports in Node.js).\n\nBecause arrow functions lock this to their\nparent scope when created, this inside greet\npoints directly to the global object.",
      "fontSize": 32.019047619047534,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Therefore, the arrow function's parent lexical scope is the global scope (window in browsers, {} or module exports in Node.js).\n\nBecause arrow functions lock this to their parent scope when created, this inside greet points directly to the global object.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9koSCxNwCNkusP0A7LGyG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8817.981805112222,
      "y": -3030.820025808782,
      "width": 372.8852538913774,
      "height": 283.8995097747513,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5fw",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 45540868,
      "version": 5646,
      "versionNonce": 2105285636,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788372684101,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The arrow function asks:\n\"Who is my enclosing lexical\nscope?\"\nIt looks at the { ... } of user.\nAn object literal is not a\nfunction or a block scope; it\nis just an assignment\nexpression sitting in the\nglobal scope.",
      "fontSize": 25.235511979977897,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The arrow function asks: \"Who is my enclosing lexical scope?\"\nIt looks at the { ... } of user. An object literal is not a function or a block scope; it is just an assignment expression sitting in the global scope.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KjrtXbpdckAjG40A2D4Kt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7306.200949636131,
      "y": -2923.677168665925,
      "width": 789.3385185185131,
      "height": 136.49999999999983,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5fx",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 478005892,
      "version": 5085,
      "versionNonce": 463880324,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788371409332,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here this refers to the person because the\nnormal function have its own this and it\nrefres to where it is created",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here this refers to the person because the normal function have its own this and it refres to where it is created",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TnP2JkC7Yvfefz56iePow",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8013.462854398034,
      "y": 516.5609265721707,
      "width": 541.6660121497126,
      "height": 366.1666666666666,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 308442044,
      "version": 2438,
      "versionNonce": 1955841340,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788364418342,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "inside test():\n\nLook for x in test's environment.\nNot found.\nGo to the outer environment.\nFind x.\nUse 10.\n\nThis is called the scope chain.",
      "fontSize": 32.548148148148144,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "inside test():\n\nLook for x in test's environment.\nNot found.\nGo to the outer environment.\nFind x.\nUse 10.\n\nThis is called the scope chain.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Qf0MWHhvq2_jSQXEODQOc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8581.796187731368,
      "y": 516.5609265721707,
      "width": 678.3326788163822,
      "height": 406.85185185185173,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 876176772,
      "version": 2928,
      "versionNonce": 618642876,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788364418342,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "scope chain\n\nIt basically it like two --> one --> global\n\nnow it find a in the two (not find) then\ngo one step up (not find) then go one\nstep up it find it at the global scope and\nprint it. and this is how it works\n\n",
      "fontSize": 32.548148148148144,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "scope chain\n\nIt basically it like two --> one --> global\n\nnow it find a in the two (not find) then go one step up (not find) then go one step up it find it at the global scope and print it. and this is how it works\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xSu31P4GkWAX3OCBkUn6q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5422.762486772484,
      "y": 449.01190476190527,
      "width": 1433.0051851851817,
      "height": 227.49999999999972,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 662334852,
      "version": 2073,
      "versionNonce": 1234105276,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788363574222,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now the answer is A B C why ?\n\nBecause first global execution start A print then when it call the test() we get\ntest in the call stack and global execution is paused then we get B and when\ntest() is finished then GE run again and we get C",
      "fontSize": 36.399999999999956,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now the answer is A B C why ?\n\nBecause first global execution start A print then when it call the test() we get test in the call stack and global execution is paused then we get B and when test() is finished then GE run again and we get C",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
